/T (When taking off the gloves, avoid touching the outer contaminated surface. Slowly pull one glove off while turning it inside out \(Figure 2a\). Place the glove in the palm of the other gloved hand \(Figure 2b\), and then remove the second glove while turning it inside out \(Figure 2c\).  )
/E (When taking off the gloves, avoid touching the outer contaminated surface. Slowly pull one glove off while turning it inside out \(Figure 2a\). Place the glove in the palm of the other gloved hand \(Figure 2b\), and then remove the second glove while turning it inside out \(Figure 2c\).  )
