/T (1. B     Ensuring the safety of the scene is critical. Avoid making yourself another injured/ill      person.  2. D      Personal protective equipment is essential when responding to any first aid or        emergency situation. It is difficult to predict if the person will vomit, is bleeding, or is        seriously injured. 3. B      Vigorously rub your hands together using soap and water for at least 20 seconds and        rinse thoroughly before and after every episode of care.)
/E (1. B     Ensuring the safety of the scene is critical. Avoid making yourself another injured/ill      person.  2. D      Personal protective equipment is essential when responding to any first aid or        emergency situation. It is difficult to predict if the person will vomit, is bleeding, or is        seriously injured. 3. B      Vigorously rub your hands together using soap and water for at least 20 seconds and        rinse thoroughly before and after every episode of care.)
