/T (Do not attempt to restrain a victim having a seizure. Also, do not try to open their mouth or put anything between their teeth. A victim experiencing an absence or staring-type seizure will have their eyes open but will not  respond to you. These episodes are generally brief and not associated with jerky body motion or loss  of consciousness. This type of event should be treated like any other seizure and a medical evaluation  is warranted.)
