/T (Seizures result in abnormal body motion due to an irregular electrical discharge in the brain. Seizures can involve one or both sides of the body. Many seizures result in rhythmic jerking motions, but some seizures may result in a blank stare type of behavior. A victim having a seizure may fall to the ground, bite their tongue, and lose control of bowel and bladder. Seizures are often accompanied by a brief period of unresponsiveness. Causes of seizures or seizure-like activity include epilepsy, low blood sugar, head injury or trauma,  heart disease, ingestion of a toxin, or heat-related illness.)
/E (Seizures result in abnormal body motion due to an irregular electrical discharge in the brain. Seizures can involve one or both sides of the body. Many seizures result in rhythmic jerking motions, but some seizures may result in a blank stare type of behavior. A victim having a seizure may fall to the ground, bite their tongue, and lose control of bowel and bladder. Seizures are often accompanied by a brief period of unresponsiveness. Causes of seizures or seizure-like activity include epilepsy, low blood sugar, head injury or trauma,  heart disease, ingestion of a toxin, or heat-related illness.)
