/P 578 0 R
/T (If a more serious injury to the eye is suspected, call 911/EMS. Protect both  eyes with a bandage or eye shield. Because the eyes work in pairs, leaving one  eye uncovered causes both eyes to move when the good eye tracks objects. Covering both eyes minimizes the movement of the injured eye. However, doing so leaves the person effectively blind, which can be dangerous and frightening to the person. Never leave a person with both eyes bandaged alone. They will require verbal cues about their environment around them as well as reassurance. A physician skilled in eye care must evaluate these injuries.)
/E (If a more serious injury to the eye is suspected, call 911/EMS. Protect both  eyes with a bandage or eye shield. Because the eyes work in pairs, leaving one  eye uncovered causes both eyes to move when the good eye tracks objects. Covering both eyes minimizes the movement of the injured eye. However, doing so leaves the person effectively blind, which can be dangerous and frightening to the person. Never leave a person with both eyes bandaged alone. They will require verbal cues about their environment around them as well as reassurance. A physician skilled in eye care must evaluate these injuries.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [7]
>>
