/T (1. Assess scene safety, wear protective equipment, and obtain first aid kit and AED. 2. Use a spray bottle with cold water and a fan, if available, as rapid cooling is imperative.       Immerse them in a cool bath or shower if available. 3. If the person is able, encourage them to drink water, a sports drink, or an electrolyte       solution. 4. Continue to cool the person until their behavior returns to normal or until advanced       help arrives.)
/E (1. Assess scene safety, wear protective equipment, and obtain first aid kit and AED. 2. Use a spray bottle with cold water and a fan, if available, as rapid cooling is imperative.       Immerse them in a cool bath or shower if available. 3. If the person is able, encourage them to drink water, a sports drink, or an electrolyte       solution. 4. Continue to cool the person until their behavior returns to normal or until advanced       help arrives.)
