/P 584 0 R
/T (Snakebites require medical attention. If the pain is getting worse, swelling occurs, bruising  develops, or systemic signs \(nausea and vomiting\) develop, a venomous snakebite has occurred. Call  911/EMS and do not delay medical attention. Make sure the scene is safe, and the snake is no longer  a threat. Keep the person calm and try to avoid moving the extremity that was bitten. Remove any  constricting clothing and jewelry from the affected area. Gently wash the affected area with soap and  water if available. Additional care is required in a hospital setting. Do not apply a tourniquet.)
/E (Snakebites require medical attention. If the pain is getting worse, swelling occurs, bruising  develops, or systemic signs \(nausea and vomiting\) develop, a venomous snakebite has occurred. Call  911/EMS and do not delay medical attention. Make sure the scene is safe, and the snake is no longer  a threat. Keep the person calm and try to avoid moving the extremity that was bitten. Remove any  constricting clothing and jewelry from the affected area. Gently wash the affected area with soap and  water if available. Additional care is required in a hospital setting. Do not apply a tourniquet.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [9 10]
>>
