/T (1. Call 911/EMS. 2. Ensure the scene is safe and wear personal protective equipment. 3. Get the first aid kit and the AED. 4. Tell the dispatcher the chemicals involved if possible. 5. Remove the person from the toxin or poison and seek a well-ventilated area if possible. 6. Remove saturated clothing if present. 7. Follow any recommendations from the 911/EMS dispatcher or the MSDS sheet. 8. Stay with the person until advanced help arrives. 9. If CPR is required, ensure a mask is used if possible.)
/E (1. Call 911/EMS. 2. Ensure the scene is safe and wear personal protective equipment. 3. Get the first aid kit and the AED. 4. Tell the dispatcher the chemicals involved if possible. 5. Remove the person from the toxin or poison and seek a well-ventilated area if possible. 6. Remove saturated clothing if present. 7. Follow any recommendations from the 911/EMS dispatcher or the MSDS sheet. 8. Stay with the person until advanced help arrives. 9. If CPR is required, ensure a mask is used if possible.)
