/P 595 0 R
/T (C Call your local EMS number or send someone to get help after determining that a victim is unresponsive. B Compression only CPR has been shown to be effective. Leaving the victim significantly  increases mortality. D Chest compressions are always given first. Breaths are performed afterward. Give two breaths  for every 30 chest compressions in an adult. B Do not stop to check a pulse after a shock is delivered. 911 or EMS should have already  been summoned. Always start with chest compressions after a shock has been delivered. C The color change suggests that they are choking. Patients who are intoxicated are at an  increased risk of choking and aspirating food contents.)
/E (C Call your local EMS number or send someone to get help after determining that a victim is unresponsive. B Compression only CPR has been shown to be effective. Leaving the victim significantly  increases mortality. D Chest compressions are always given first. Breaths are performed afterward. Give two breaths  for every 30 chest compressions in an adult. B Do not stop to check a pulse after a shock is delivered. 911 or EMS should have already  been summoned. Always start with chest compressions after a shock has been delivered. C The color change suggests that they are choking. Patients who are intoxicated are at an  increased risk of choking and aspirating food contents.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [7]
>>
