/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 600 0 R
/T (1. Turn the power on \(Figure 22a\). 2. Expose the chest \(Figure 22b\). 3. Apply pads on the child. Ensure that the pads do not touch \(Figure 22c, Figure 22d \). 4. Connect the pads \(Figure 22e\). 5. Clear the child so no one is touching the child. 6. Analyze the rhythm. 7. Follow the prompts: Shock Advised, No Shock Advised, Check Connection, etc. 8. Resume CPR with compressions \(Figure 22f\). )
/E (1. Turn the power on \(Figure 22a\). 2. Expose the chest \(Figure 22b\). 3. Apply pads on the child. Ensure that the pads do not touch \(Figure 22c, Figure 22d \). 4. Connect the pads \(Figure 22e\). 5. Clear the child so no one is touching the child. 6. Analyze the rhythm. 7. Follow the prompts: Shock Advised, No Shock Advised, Check Connection, etc. 8. Resume CPR with compressions \(Figure 22f\). )
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
