/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 604 0 R
/T (1. What is the main difference in care when finding an unresponsive adult versus an        unresponsive child if you must leave the person to activate EMS?      a. There is no difference.      b. Perform CPR first when with an adult; go for help first when with a child.      c. Perform two minutes of CPR when with a child, then go for help; call for help           immediately when with an adult.      d. It depends on the age of the child.)
/E (1. What is the main difference in care when finding an unresponsive adult versus an        unresponsive child if you must leave the person to activate EMS?      a. There is no difference.      b. Perform CPR first when with an adult; go for help first when with a child.      c. Perform two minutes of CPR when with a child, then go for help; call for help           immediately when with an adult.      d. It depends on the age of the child.)
/Pg 52 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
