/T (A Infants are considered to be less than one year of age. A child is between one year  and puberty. C If an infant becomes unresponsive during an attempt to relieve choking, position them  on a firm, flat surface, and begin CPR. B Respiratory problems usually precede cardiac arrest in both infants and children. B  Give ten cycles of 15 compressions and two breaths in an unresponsive infant before going to call 911/EMS. If someone is available to help, send them immediately to call 911/EMS.)
/E (A Infants are considered to be less than one year of age. A child is between one year  and puberty. C If an infant becomes unresponsive during an attempt to relieve choking, position them  on a firm, flat surface, and begin CPR. B Respiratory problems usually precede cardiac arrest in both infants and children. B  Give ten cycles of 15 compressions and two breaths in an unresponsive infant before going to call 911/EMS. If someone is available to help, send them immediately to call 911/EMS.)
