/T (Persons who have asthma or chronic lung disease are generally familiar on how to use their breathing medications. Common medications include albuterol and Atrovent inhalers. The use of a spacer \(a tube attached to the inhaler that holds the medication until the victim breathes it in\) can improve the effect of these medications. A person in severe distress may be unable to properly use their inhaler. Call 911/EMS if the person appears in significant distress.)
/E (Persons who have asthma or chronic lung disease are generally familiar on how to use their breathing medications. Common medications include albuterol and Atrovent inhalers. The use of a spacer \(a tube attached to the inhaler that holds the medication until the victim breathes it in\) can improve the effect of these medications. A person in severe distress may be unable to properly use their inhaler. Call 911/EMS if the person appears in significant distress.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K []
>>
